Thanks for the references! I'm aware of these related issues — this is intentionally reopening #1167 which was auto-closed due to inactivity, not resolved.
I've already implemented the fix and have a PR ready to submit. The change binds ctrl+backspace to deleteWordBackward in the TUI keybindings. The opencode package typechecks cleanly.
@simonklee happy to submit the PR now if you'd like to review it!

@thdxr Why have you removed the bug and ACP flag? 

Seriously folks, i appreciate that managing that many contributions is not easy, but this experience is really awful. I've waited for two months without getting any feedback, fixed merge conflicts over that period in my PR as new code got merged, only to see my ticket essentially made irrelevant without getting any feedback.

This is not a way to treat contributors.

@Milor123 

The error is coming from your chat template. Your `S:\DownloadsWIN\chat_template.jinja` still has the upstream guard at line 116:

> {%- if not loop.first %}
     {{- raise_exception('System message must be at the beginning.') }}

Interestingly there has been another update to the fixed template. I would now suggest you use the following: 

- https://huggingface.co/froggeric/Qwen-Fixed-Chat-Templates/blob/781cc5152b46bacba17fd1aadbea5049d8d490f1/qwen3.6/chat_template-v8.jinja

Will also test that one once I find some time 😉
